WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:01.310
Take that!

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.990
<i>The Earth is being targeted.</i>

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.730
<i>A horrifying invasion force is 
now making its way towards Earth</i>

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.190
<i>from the countless planets that 
drift in the vastness of space.</i>

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:39.560
Welcome to the Astronomy Club.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.560
Have a seat over there.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.000
What did you come here for?

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.090
I'm looking for a certain someone.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:54.850
I've researched your club here.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.580
The pun in the name is stupid.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:58.310
Why put "agonizing" in there at all?

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.120
I see you're still wasting your 
time with pointless frivolities.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.690
I wouldn't have come here 
if I didn't have to.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.130
Wh-What?

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:18.510
You're here now, so relax a little.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.700
This scent...

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:27.520
Todayama...

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.550
Yes, you quite liked it, didn't you?

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:34.530
It has a calming effect 
that helps you relax.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.550
It can also be used for hypnosis.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:40.950
You tricked me!

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.420
I will have anyone who 
gets in my way disappear.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.100
Return to your original world.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:23.080
<b>Put Love Into It, Not Konpeito</b>

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:56.400
<b>Earth Defense Forces Headquarters</b>

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.760
This is an emergency.

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:02.880
Listen up, everyone.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:08.680
The enemy has sent us, 
the Earth Defense Forces, a challenge!

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.140
E-Enemy?

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.560
And the Earth Defense Forces are 
supposed to be who exactly?

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.720
Anyway, I've gone ahead 
and captured the enemy.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.820
We're going to observe her for a while.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.570
That's our enemy?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.400
Where's her uniform from?

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.140
She's from a different school?

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.360
I don't think she wants 
to invade anything.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:33.280
Did she come here by mistake?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.920
<b>Earth Defense Forces Headquarters</b>

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.920
<b>Prisoner of War</b>

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.630
Welcome to the Astronomy Club.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:43.340
Thank you...

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.720
Nice to meet you.

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.340
I'm the Vice President here, Ooba.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.270
Did you want to join our club?

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.810
No, that's not it!

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:59.010
Things kind of ended up this way.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:00.860
Is that so?

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:04.420
Well, we welcome anyone that comes

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.030
to our Astronomy Club.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:07.900
Stop it!

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:09.500
Don't let her fool you!

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.190
The aliens are trying to invade!

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.230
It's a trap!

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:14.280
Leave our planet!

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.610
This is good.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.960
You're complete surround—

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:16.960
I'm glad you like it.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.580
You're very nice.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.110
I thought everyone here was weird.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:23.470
Like her.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:27.720
Don't worry about her. 
She won't harm you.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.090
Hey! That's rude!

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:32.730
Oh, I have an idea.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:35.420
Would you like to shadow 
our club today?

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.270
Huh?

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.150
You can't, Vice President!

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.050
She's an alien!

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.320
Do you not care what happens 
to our Astronomy Club?!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.770
She doesn't look like an alien to me.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:47.240
And that's exactly her plan!

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.050
The flying saucers are here!

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:51.660
The aliens are here!

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:53.910
I'll take her out!

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:09.840
I don't plan on losing in a 
contest of brute strength.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.590
What was that?!

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.050
She stopped Todayama?

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.190
You arrogant bitch!

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:19.850
That alien's pretty good.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:22.400
I told you I'm not an alien...

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.140
You managed to avoid the brunt 
of Todayama's craziness—

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:27.780
an impossibility for someone 
new to dealing with her.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:29.710
Who are you, exactly?

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:31.530
Why did you come to the Astronomy Club?

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:35.310
I told you I was looking for someone.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.560
Looking for someone?

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.290
Watch out, Hiromatsu!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.540
Everything this girl says is bull!

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.170
Why don't you go look in the mirror?!

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.570
Go back to outer space!

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.550
The Astronomy Club 
belongs to the Tonmaln!

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:51.410
If you try to invade, 
things won't go that well for you!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:52.310
What are you talking about?

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:53.700
You're not making sense.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.620
I don't know who you're searching for,

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.900
but if that's important, 
why not just take a look around.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:06:59.560
Huh?

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:01.470
You looking for her?

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:02.140
No.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:03.870
Up next.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:05.080
No.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:06.920
All that's left is...

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:09.720
A cat?

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.480
Yeah, this is Oomori-sensei.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:12.740
A-A teacher?

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.110
She's our club advisor. 
Is there a problem?

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:16.450
Right...

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.870
Anyway, I know that they're here!

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:24.220
Why go to a school with you in it?!

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:28.230
There's something fishy about this.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.090
Where are...

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:30.970
...you...

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.220
...keeping them?!

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.260
Now this just looks weird.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.670
I wouldn't open that.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:45.360
Come on... What is this stuff?

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:48.030
The "Forbidden Story 
of Two Former Brothers:

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.450
Me, 'Traman, and Baltan Appear."

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.670
Stop it!

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.680
Don't look! Don't touch!

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.270
You're looking straight at 
a woman's precious treasure,

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:00.040
You mean filled with the 
filth of a fujoshi...

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:01.370
filled with flowers and stuff.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.370
I tried to tell you.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.520
There must be a clue somewhere.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.510
Hey! Stop it!

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:10.970
Don't go there! Don't touch that!

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:12.310
It's going to go all over!

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:22.470
Look at what you did...

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.740
Konpeito?

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.060
<i>If I could get the human body</i>

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:37.210
<i>to recognize this as 
an organic compound,</i>

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:41.330
<i>I should be able to control the 
activation of certain enzymes.</i>

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.780
<i>For example, we know that 
the chemical formula</i>

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:48.960
<i>for diphenhydramine is C17H21NO.</i>

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.280
<i>Diphenhydramine HCl 
has, as a side effect,</i>

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:54.720
<i>strong sedative properties that 
many acknowledge as a problem...</i>

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.690
<i>There she is. It's that girl.</i>

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.420
<i>Todayama-san's kinda...</i>

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:02.070
<i>She's totally weird.</i>

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.590
<i>If you get too close to 
her, she'll kill you.</i>

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.610
<i>...Promethazine... Ketotifen...</i>

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:08.710
<i>They all act on the 
histamine H1 receptors,</i>

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:10.290
<i>which is expressed by neurotransmitters</i>

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.860
<i>throughout the central nervous system.</i>

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:17.010
<i>And if I can use a histamine antagonist</i>

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:20.160
<i>as a test to stimulate 
a sedative response,</i>

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.550
<i>then I just might be able to...</i>

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.630
That's right. Ever since then,

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:37.690
I've had to constantly 
deal with your nonsense...

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:40.080
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.180
You're always taking the 
things that are dear to me.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:49.480
You were the main reason 
why I lost my friends.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.300
Right...

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:58.990
Just stop causing problems 
for me already, Onee-sama!

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:02.150
What?!

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:03.670
What? O-Onee-sama?

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:06.330
Huh? I didn't tell you guys?

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:12.040
<b>How's Oomori-sensei (the person) today?</b>

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:15.280
Yeah, I'm having less 
and less to do lately.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.300
The commander's getting pretty mad.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.300
But it's fine.

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:24.100
It's the mission of a 
woman to live for love.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:34.550
Hey, honey, what are 
you doing right now?

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:50.860
So that's what you're up to?

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:52.470
Sounds like fun.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:55.980
Take me with you next time.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:57.570
Promise, okay?

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:59.180
Bye.

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:08.040
I have to make lunch for him.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.370
I better get going.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:12.980
<b>To be continued</b>

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.370
To be continued!

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:19.490
She's your... younger sister?

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:22.620
Oh, this is Todayama Izumiko.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.540
My younger sister that's a first-year.

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:26.180
She goes to a different school, though.

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.750
Why is she here at our school?

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:32.960
From the look of things, 
she doesn't seem to like you.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:35.650
I don't think she came here simply to

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:37.480
come and see her wonderful sister.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:39.260
That's not true!

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.550
Izumiko and I were known 
throughout our neighborhood as

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:42.110
<b>The Todayama Sisters</b>

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:43.510
beautiful sisters who were best friends.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.050
She just said she was beautiful 
without even flinching!

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:48.730
You missed the part where 
she said "were known."

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:50.140
You know, past tense.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:55.530
It's true that we were 
thought of like that.

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:57.740
But...

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:03.180
<i>So that's the constellation.</i>

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:08.480
<i>You're not going to sleep yet?</i>

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.160
<i>I will in a bit.</i>

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.490
<i>You sure get focused on things.</i>

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:17.800
<i>You're going to freeze out here.</i>

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:19.780
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:21.710
<i>Oh, yeah...</i>

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:23.680
<i>Want one?</i>

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.310
<i>How pretty!</i>

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:32.560
<i>That large white star there is Sirius.</i>

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:36.710
<i>It has the same name as that 
sparkling star over there.</i>

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:37.820
<i>Sirius?</i>

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:41.570
<i>That's right. It's the largest star.</i>

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:45.430
<i>There's countless secrets 
hiding in each star,</i>

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:47.240
<i>just like the one you see there.</i>

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:50.850
<i>If I can figure out those 
secrets through my research,</i>

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.850
I'm sure Onee-sama will 
be able to do anything.

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:52.240
She's a genius.

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:53.380
<i>I'm sure everything'll go just fine.</i>

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:56.420
<i>This smells good.</i>

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:58.970
<i>Go ahead and eat it</i>

00:12:58.970 --> 00:12:59.790
<i>Okay.</i>

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.180
<i>It's good!</i>

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.430
<i>There you go.</i>

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.390
<i>Izumiko, do you believe in fate?</i>

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:15.360
<i>I don't know...</i>

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:20.820
<i>Yeah... That's for the best.</i>

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.550
I loved her.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.820
She was beautiful, 
smart... but then she...

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:33.640
<i>Onee-sama, why are you trying to leave?</i>

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:39.730
<i>Izumiko, I'm not a normal person.</i>

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:43.420
<i>I have exceeded the 
concept that defined me—</i>

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:45.260
<i>I am a traveler of fate!</i>

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:50.170
<i>I know you're surprised.</i>

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:53.520
<i>What are you saying?</i>

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:57.850
<i>It doesn't matter who you are, 
you're still my sister.</i>

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.260
<i>Thank you, Izumiko.</i>

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:02.530
<i>I must return to that star,</i>

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:04.340
<i>to save this world using konpeito.</i>

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:04.860
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:05.180 --> 00:14:08.170
<i>When the Morning Star sparkles 
in the Eastern sky,</i>

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:10.500
<i>a single light will continue 
flying towards the cosmos.</i>

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:11.870
<i>And that light will be me.</i>

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:14.770
<i>Farewell, Izumiko.</i>

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:16.240
<i>Wait, Onee-sama!</i>

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:17.040
<i>Don't go!</i>

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:18.740
<i>You're embarrassing me,</i>

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:20.540
<i>so stop saying stuff like that outside!</i>

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:22.510
<i>The world is in peril!</i>

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:25.270
<i>Now is the time for the stars 
to let off their power!</i>

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:28.900
<i>I'll end this story with my own hands.</i>

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:31.430
<i>Star Soldier: Legend!</i>

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:33.940
<i>Pop!</i>

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:37.330
Onee-sama said a lot of things 
that didn't make any sense.

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:39.150
She said it was because she 
didn't want to get a shot,

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:41.110
or made something up about konpeito...

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.500
But at any rate, she had become infected

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.690
with the all so contagious 
"chuunibyou" syndrome.

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:47.490
Chuunibyou?

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.200
I think everyone goes through that.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.910
All right, Izumiko!

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.390
I will not allow you to disrupt

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:54.160
the Astronomy Club's 
activities any further!

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.820
If you cannot pass the test I give you,

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:58.040
you're going back to Kyoto!

00:14:58.320 --> 00:14:59.560
Activities?

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:02.500
You're not really doing 
anything anyway, right?

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:04.800
Don't make fun of the Astronomy Club!

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:06.450
Yeah, I wonder just what

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.590
type of weird things you're 
doing down here in the basement.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:11.090
You want to know? Take the quiz.

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:13.750
Fine! You're on.

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:16.020
But in exchange, if I pass your test,

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:17.730
you'll let me see the 
person I'm looking for.

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:18.930
Sounds good to me.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:21.860
Sorry I just got here.

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:24.650
You're later than usual today.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:27.050
Yeah, sorry. I was on cleaning duty.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.460
Let's get started.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.030
First question of the club entry test.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:46.710
Five Oaths of the Astronomy Club 
 1. Don't just look at the BBS 
and take what they say at face value. 
2. It's not parody. It's respect.
3. Put your dakimakura out when the weather's good.
4. Who's Oomori-sensei's boyfriend, anyway?
5. Go ahead and upload ____ videos of Kanamori to Nico.

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:39.560
These are the five oaths that anyone who

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:41.700
enters into the Astronomy Club makes.

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:44.110
Fill in the blank.

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:46.710
All of those oaths are weird.

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:49.500
What goes in the blank?

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:51.220
Fun!

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.720
Buzz, buzz.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.870
Like we wouldn't go 
further than that.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:56.510
Don't make light of the Astronomy Club!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.770
<b>Naked</b>

00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:59.770
The correct answer was "naked videos."

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:00.720
What?!

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:01.800
Hey, Kanamori!

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:02.700
Yeah?

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.270
Show them how serious we are.

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:08.020
No!

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:12.630
<b>Serious!</b>

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.590
There we go!

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:10.000
You know this feels right!

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:12.950
Look at how cute you are!

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:14.780
What's that sound?

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:17.120
President

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.490
What's going on here?!

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:22.200
This Astronomy Club smells suspicious.

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:24.750
Is it true you guys got another 
person who wants to join?

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:27.420
Student Council President Iseda...

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.670
I never would have 
expected another enemy

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.900
would find their way here 
when all of this is going on.

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:35.590
Is that your new member?!

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.170
No, she's not.

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:39.360
Calm down a little, President Iseda.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:40.430
Huh? Really?

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:42.730
Okay, we're using this 
chance to get out of here!

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:45.890
Huh? Wait! Wait! Wait!

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:48.300
Give me back my clothes!

00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:47.360
Hey!

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:50.360
It's cold!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.720
Hey, wait!

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:55.660
Huh... I still...

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.160
What is this place?

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.920
It's our secret escape route.

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:02.790
Every clubroom has one.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:03.980
I don't think that's right.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:06.380
We, the Astronomy Club, at times

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:08.050
must fight against aliens.

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:11.450
Not to mention a certain sister-robot 
that came from Planet 5.

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:13.920
I told you I'm not an alien...

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:18.430
All aliens say the same thing, 
that they're not aliens.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:21.430
Then what am I supposed to say?!

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:25.300
You're always saying things 
that don't make sense to me.

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:28.190
You never tell me anything straight.

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:33.820
When did you become such... a weirdo?!

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:37.070
Good job, sister.

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.680
Todayama's surprisingly taking a lot

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:40.330
of critical damage from that hit.

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:44.710
Insulting me is akin to 
insulting the Astronomy Club.

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:45.960
Is it?

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:48.120
If being insulted makes you so upset,

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:51.720
how about saying something 
normal for once?

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:55.530
You jerk!

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:02.590
We're settling this, Izumiko.

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:03.970
Fine.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.650
If you win against me, 
I'll let you do whatever you want.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.710
However, if you lose,

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:14.020
you will never be allowed to 
visit the Astronomy Club again!

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:15.650
Sounds just fine to me.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.160
Agonizing Astronomy Club's Escape Door

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.540
Take this!

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:24.910
Take this!

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:27.660
Why don't you understand how I feel?!

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:30.040
Shut up already! All you do is cry!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.680
When do I cry?!

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.050
All the time!

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.510
You're always like this!

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:37.300
What the hell are you talking about?

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:40.510
You took my pink ribbon from me, 
even though I really liked it,

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:42.590
because you thought it 
looked better on you!

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:44.890
You told me you liked the red one!

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:45.930
How long ago was that anyway?!

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.730
Kindergarten!

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:49.900
Kindergarten?!

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:53.100
I'll never forget when you 
kept calling me "Piko."

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:55.720
How many times did you 
wet my bed when you were

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:58.450
sleeping because you couldn't 
go to the bathroom by yourself?!

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:00.360
I-I don't remember anything like that!

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.370
You're a bed wetter, Izumiko!

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.420
You couldn't stand losing 
against me in a game,

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:06.010
so you'd always press reset on

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:08.180
the console before you died!

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:09.990
Yeah, well, you couldn't even 
say spaghetti right until

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:15.460
<b>Miniature park</b>

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:11.910
you got into elementary school! 
You kept saying "splagetti!"

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:13.210
So basically this episode...

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.460
Is just two sisters having an argument?

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:17.970
Take this!

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:29.310
That was underhanded!

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:32.520
That smells like...

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:44.470
Good night, Izumiko.

00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:49.140
<i>And so the Astronomy Club 
was safe for another day.</i>

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:53.440
<i>Thank you, Todayama, 
Club Member of Justice.</i>

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:57.010
Actually... Where's Noya-san?

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:58.920
Hey!

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.580
Hey!

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:08.270
The president took the vice president.

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:10.770
I bet she's going to go off about how

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:12.620
the club needs to be shut down again.

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:13.690
I feel bad for her.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:17.120
Todayama's sister still 
hasn't woken up.

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:20.080
Oh, it's almost time for her to get up.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:21.360
How can you tell?

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:25.630
I used some special incense today.

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:26.740
Huh?

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.540
You mean that was...

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:35.630
I saw on TV a long time 
ago an alien that used

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.830
the smoke from cigarettes 
to control people...

00:20:38.980 --> 00:20:41.800
It's hard work to keep up 
with her, too, you know?

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:45.650
So basically, in the end, you just 
had your fun playing with her?

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:46.800
So nothing really different than usual.

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:50.830
It looks like she's up.

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:52.990
Wh-Where am I...

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:54.730
What was I...

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:55.520
Oh—

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:58.740
It's better that you don't remember.

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:03.020
I'll leave things be, 
so just head home.

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:05.550
If you don't,

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:08.090
I'll upload some of the 
embarrassing photos here

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:10.380
all over the net.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:16.110
<i>Embarrassing photos?</i>

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:18.570
<i>Did she have me dress up and take</i>

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:21.090
<i>pictures for her while I was asleep?!</i>

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:25.510
<i>Knowing her, I wouldn't be 
surprised if she did...</i>

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:30.280
Fine, Onee-sama.

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:33.380
I'll just head back.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:44.210
<i>Thank you, Izumiko.</i>

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:47.720
I'll talk to you later, Onee-sama.

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:48.470
Yeah.

00:21:50.360 --> 00:21:53.960
We might see each other again soon.

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:54.870
Huh?

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:57.320
Make sure you stay well until then.

00:22:03.640 --> 00:22:07.300
<i>I know Onee-sama is hiding something.</i>

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:11.000
<i>I need to look into this further.</i>

00:22:11.770 --> 00:22:15.120
<i>But where was...</i>

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:17.490
<i>Itsuki-sama?</i>

00:22:18.620 --> 00:22:19.900
Oh, a shooting star.

00:22:20.570 --> 00:22:22.990
The stars are pretty today, too.

00:22:22.990 --> 00:22:26.290
So why did your sister have 
a car come to pick her up,

00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:28.410
but you're walking home?

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:31.260
We're not living in the 
same place right now.

00:22:31.260 --> 00:22:33.460
Huh? Wh-What's going on?

00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:35.410
Did something happen?

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:39.460
You said Kyoto, too...

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:41.320
Is that where your parents' house is?

00:22:54.490 --> 00:22:56.090
The Earth is being targeted.

00:24:30.780 --> 00:24:32.150
Astronomy Club, deploy!

00:24:32.150 --> 00:24:33.780
Planetarium, open!

00:24:33.780 --> 00:24:35.120
Neko-sensei, launch!

00:24:33.800 --> 00:24:35.100
Please do not fire Neko-sensei at others

00:24:35.540 --> 00:24:37.910
Your own high-tech Astronomy 
Club clubhouse!

00:24:36.180 --> 00:24:37.890
<b>Deluxe Astronomy Club clubhouse</b>

00:24:37.910 --> 00:24:39.530
Comes with an illustrated 
book with all the members!

00:24:38.970 --> 00:24:40.270
Next Time: 
Stamp 2012 
Look forward to it!
